course: dictionary
lesson: 14973
title: Remuneration means pay
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Remuneration is a formal word for money paid to someone for their work. It means pay or wages. «Her remuneration for mowing the lawns was five pounds.» The clue is that she was paid money for a job, so remuneration must mean pay.
explain: You will often meet remuneration in exam questions and business writing, where grown-ups use longer, stiffer words than in everyday talk. In a maths problem, «the remuneration is $15 per hour» means the worker is paid $15 for every hour.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping in a simpler word. «The remuneration is $15 per hour» becomes «The pay is $15 per hour», and it still makes sense, so pay is the right meaning. Pay and wages are the everyday words you can use instead.
fact: Remuneration is a noun. You can say «remuneration» on its own, or «a remuneration».
fact: «Remuneration» means money paid to someone for work.
fact: Everyday synonyms for remuneration are pay and wages.
fact: A «remuneration package» is the pay offered for a job.
fact: «Total remuneration» means all the money someone earns from a job, added together.
exercise: «The gardener's remuneration was ten pounds for the afternoon.» What does remuneration mean here? | A long rest after lunch | A tool for digging | *Money paid for work | A garden full of flowers
exercise: «Mia's wages for the summer job were paid on Friday.» Find and copy one word that means the same as remuneration. | uniform | *wages | summer | holiday
exercise: In a maths problem, «the remuneration is $15 per hour.» What does the worker get? | *$15 for every hour worked | A free lunch every hour | A new uniform | Fifteen hours off work
test: «The company offered her a generous remuneration package.» What is a remuneration package? | *The pay offered for a job | A list of the workers' names | A box of tools for the job | A map of the office
test: Ravi says remuneration is just a fancy way of saying pay. Is he right? | No, it means the place where people work | No, it means a rule that workers must follow | No, it means a holiday from work | *Yes, remuneration means money paid for work
exam: «His total remuneration for the year was all the money he earned from his job.» What does total remuneration mean? | The cost of his tools | The number of hours he worked | *All the money earned from a job, added together | The name of his company
